        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-[var(--text-muted)] leading-relaxed">
          Torsion-spring hand grippers are a widely adopted benchmark of crushing power, but stamped factory numbers create immense confusion. Here is the engineering science behind why manufacturer ratings mislead, how the RGC system standardizes closing force, and why calibration is essential.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- 3-Column Explainer Grid -->
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        
        <!-- Card 1: The Problem with Factory Ratings -->
        <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-[var(--bg-surface)] border border-[var(--border-color)] flex flex-col justify-between shadow-sm">
          <div>
            <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-red-500/10 text-red-500 flex items-center justify-center font-mono font-bold text-sm mb-4 border border-red-500/20">
              01
            </div>
            <h3 class="font-display font-bold text-lg uppercase text-[var(--text-main)] mb-2">
              Why Factory Numbers Mislead
            </h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-[var(--text-muted)] leading-relaxed">
              When a brand advertises a gripper as <strong>"195 lbs" (like a CoC #2)</strong> or <strong>"280 lbs" (CoC #3)</strong>, that number represents either theoretical spring torque, midpoint resistance, or engineering wire deflection before handle leverage is introduced.
            </p>
            <div class="mt-4 p-3 rounded-lg bg-[var(--bg-elevated)] text-[11px] font-mono text-[var(--text-subtle)] border border-[var(--border-color)]">
              Factory Stamp: ~195 lbs<br/>
              Actual Hand Resistance: ~106 lbs RGC
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-4 text-[11px] text-[var(--text-muted)] pt-3 border-t border-[var(--border-color)]">
            Human hands squeeze along the entire length of the handle, with pinky drive applying force at maximum leverage.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Card 2: The RGC Standardization Method -->
        <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-[var(--bg-surface)] border border-[var(--border-color)] flex flex-col justify-between shadow-sm">
          <div>
            <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-[var(--accent-gold)]/15 text-[var(--accent-gold)] flex items-center justify-center font-mono font-bold text-sm mb-4 border border-[var(--accent-gold)]/30">
              02
