              How RGC Is Measured
            </h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-[var(--text-muted)] leading-relaxed">
              <strong>RGC (Redneck Gripper Calibration)</strong>, pioneered by Cannon PowerWorks and adopted globally, removes all human subjectivity. The gripper is clamped horizontally by one handle into a rigid steel fixture. A 1/4" non-elastic strap is positioned precisely at the very tip of the free handle.
            </p>
            <div class="mt-4 p-3 rounded-lg bg-[var(--bg-elevated)] text-[11px] font-mono text-[var(--text-subtle)] border border-[var(--border-color)]">
              Fixture: Horizontal steel clamp<br/>
              Fulcrum: 1/4" strap at handle tip<br/>
              Target: Calibrated parallel contact
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-4 text-[11px] text-[var(--text-muted)] pt-3 border-t border-[var(--border-color)]">
            Calibrated static weight is added until the handles make parallel contact. The suspended weight in pounds is the true RGC.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Card 3: Manufacturing Tolerances & Stepping Stones -->
        <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-[var(--bg-surface)] border border-[var(--border-color)] flex flex-col justify-between shadow-sm">
