              <span class="font-bold font-mono text-[var(--accent-gold)] block uppercase mb-1">1. Rising Bar (Standard 4 Attempts)</span>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-muted)] leading-relaxed">
                The bar only goes up. The lifter with the lowest opening attempt lifts first. Once a weight is loaded, all competitors attempting that weight take their turn before the pin is increased. Lifters generally take 4 attempts per event.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="p-3 rounded-lg bg-[var(--bg-elevated)] border border-[var(--border-color)]">
              <span class="font-bold font-mono text-[var(--accent-gold)] block uppercase mb-1">2. Last Man Standing (Uniform Increments)</span>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-muted)] leading-relaxed">
                The apparatus increases by set increments every round (e.g. 1 kg / 2.5 lbs for light pinch tools like The Stub; 5 kg / 10 lbs for Axles). Lifters jump in when their desired weight is reached and stay until eliminated.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="text-[11px] text-[var(--text-muted)] p-2 border-l-2 border-[var(--accent-gold)]">
              <strong>Scoresheet Notation:</strong> Successful lifts are circled on the scorecard; missed attempts are marked with a strike-through line.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Scoring Mechanics: Grip Sport vs Strongman -->
        <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-[var(--bg-surface)] border border-[var(--border-color)] shadow-sm">
          <h3 class="font-display font-bold text-lg uppercase text-[var(--text-main)] mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-[var(--accent-gold)]"></span>
            Grip Sport vs Strongman Scoring
          </h3>
          <div class="space-y-4 text-xs">
            <div class="p-3 rounded-lg bg-emerald-500/10 border border-emerald-500/20 text-[var(--text-main)]">
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-1">
                <span class="font-bold font-mono text-emerald-500 uppercase">Grip Sport Scoring (Percentage Based)</span>
                <span class="text-[10px] font-mono text-emerald-400 font-semibold">High Points Win</span>
              </div>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-muted)] leading-relaxed">
                The event winner receives <strong>100 points</strong>. Every other competitor's score is calculated proportionally:
              </p>
              <div class="mt-2 font-mono text-[11px] bg-[var(--bg-surface)] p-2 rounded border border-emerald-500/30 text-emerald-400">
                Score = (Competitor Lift &divide; Winning Lift) &times; 100
              </div>
              <p class="text-[11px] text-[var(--text-muted)] mt-2">
                <em>Advantage:</em> Directly rewards margin of victory. Dominant lifts yield substantial point cushions.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="p-3 rounded-lg bg-[var(--bg-elevated)] border border-[var(--border-color)] text-[var(--text-main)]">
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-1">
                <span class="font-bold font-mono text-[var(--text-main)] uppercase">Strongman Scoring (Rank Placement)</span>
                <span class="text-[10px] font-mono text-[var(--text-muted)] font-semibold">Low Points Win</span>
              </div>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-muted)] leading-relaxed">
                Golf-style placement points (1st place = 1 point, 2nd place = 2 points, 3rd = 3 points). Fastest to score, but equalizes margin of victory.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>

      <!-- 24-Hour Submission Action Card -->
      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-[var(--bg-surface)] border border-[var(--accent-gold)]/40 flex flex-col md:flex-row items-start md:items-center justify-between gap-6 shadow-sm">
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-[10px] font-mono font-bold uppercase bg-amber-500/15 text-amber-500 border border-amber-500/30">
              Mandatory Post-Contest Procedure
            </span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-display font-bold text-xl uppercase text-[var(--text-main)]">
            Submit Results Within 24 Hours via Official Spreadsheet
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-[var(--text-muted)] max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
            Following contest completion, scores must be compiled using the official GSI spreadsheet template and emailed promptly to <strong>Eric Roussin</strong> (<a href="mailto:eroussin@rogers.com" class="text-[var(--accent-gold)] underline">eroussin@rogers.com</a>) and <strong>Jedd Johnson</strong> (<a href="mailto:jedd.diesel@gmail.com" class="text-[var(--accent-gold)] underline">jedd.diesel@gmail.com</a>). Reference documents and templates are published on <a href="https://gripsportint.com/resources" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[var(--accent-gold)] underline">gripsportint.com/resources</a>.
          </p>
